<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1" ProductVersion="3.1.4026.18">
  <POU Name="ListBuffer" Id="{035aeb58-d2b0-41bd-9654-fb44a8d66373}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[// Provides a directional FIFO list with automatic shift-and-overwrite when full
FUNCTION_BLOCK ListBuffer IMPLEMENTS I_AnyBufferStrategy
VAR
	anyBuffer	  : I_AnyBuffer;
	isInitialized : BOOL := FALSE;
	_reversed	  : BOOL := FALSE; // TRUE: add at left, FALSE: add at right (end)
END_VAR

(*
## Detailed Description

List is an adapter that wraps an AnyBuffer instance to provide a configurable-direction
FIFO (First-In-First-Out) list with automatic shift-and-overwrite capability. Unlike a
simple ring buffer, this implementation physically shifts elements when the buffer is full
to maintain contiguous storage and consistent indexing.

### Design Rationale
This adapter is called "List" because it provides list-like semantics:
- Elements are stored contiguously in memory
- Insertion direction can be configured (prepend vs append)
- Automatic capacity management with shift-on-overwrite
- Maintains FIFO ordering regardless of fill direction

### Design Pattern
This implements the **Adapter Pattern** with directional configuration:
- Wraps the AnyBuffer interface with configurable list semantics
- Delegates all operations to the underlying AnyBuffer instance
- Provides automatic shift-and-overwrite when buffer reaches capacity
- Uses private helper methods for clean code organization

### Directional Fill Semantics

**Fill From Left (fillFromLeft = TRUE)**:
- Push adds at index 0 (AppendLeft) - newest at front
- Pop removes from highest index (PopRight) - oldest at end
- When full: Remove oldest (PopRight), add new (AppendLeft)
- Visual: [newest] ← [older] ← [oldest]

**Fill From Right (fillFromLeft = FALSE)**:
- Push adds at end (AppendRight) - newest at end
- Pop removes from index 0 (PopLeft) - oldest at front
- When full: Remove oldest (PopLeft), add new (AppendRight)
- Visual: [oldest] → [older] → [newest]

### Operation Mapping

**When fillFromLeft = TRUE:**
```
Push() not full  -> AppendLeft()          // Add to front
Push() full      -> PopRight() + AppendLeft()  // Remove oldest (end), add new (front)
Pop()            -> PopRight()            // Remove oldest (end)
```

**When fillFromLeft = FALSE:**
```
Push() not full  -> AppendRight()         // Add to end
Push() full      -> PopLeft() + AppendRight()  // Remove oldest (front), add new (end)
Pop()            -> PopLeft()             // Remove oldest (front)
```

### Usage Example - Fill From Left

```iecst
VAR
    rawBuffer : ARRAY[0..2] OF DINT;  // 3-element buffer
    buffer : AnyBuffer(pBuffer := rawBuffer,
                       bufferBoundLower := 0,
                       bufferBoundUpper := 2,
                       isBufferPersistent := FALSE);
    list : List(anyBuffer := buffer, fillFromLeft := TRUE);
    value : DINT;
END_VAR

// Fill from left (prepend)
value := 100; list.Push(value);  // Buffer: [100]
value := 200; list.Push(value);  // Buffer: [200, 100]
value := 300; list.Push(value);  // Buffer: [300, 200, 100] - Full

// Push to full buffer - oldest (100) removed, new prepended
value := 400; list.Push(value);  // Buffer: [400, 300, 200]
value := 500; list.Push(value);  // Buffer: [500, 400, 300]

// Pop removes oldest (from end)
list.Pop(value);  // value = 300, Buffer: [500, 400]
list.Pop(value);  // value = 400, Buffer: [500]
```

### Usage Example - Fill From Right

```iecst
VAR
    rawBuffer : ARRAY[0..2] OF DINT;  // 3-element buffer
    buffer : AnyBuffer(pBuffer := rawBuffer,
                       bufferBoundLower := 0,
                       bufferBoundUpper := 2,
                       isBufferPersistent := FALSE);
    list : List(anyBuffer := buffer, fillFromLeft := FALSE);
    value : DINT;
END_VAR

// Fill from right (append)
value := 100; list.Push(value);  // Buffer: [100]
value := 200; list.Push(value);  // Buffer: [100, 200]
value := 300; list.Push(value);  // Buffer: [100, 200, 300] - Full

// Push to full buffer - oldest (100) removed, new appended
value := 400; list.Push(value);  // Buffer: [200, 300, 400]
value := 500; list.Push(value);  // Buffer: [300, 400, 500]

// Pop removes oldest (from front)
list.Pop(value);  // value = 300, Buffer: [400, 500]
list.Pop(value);  // value = 400, Buffer: [500]
```

### Shift-and-Overwrite Visualization (fillFromLeft = FALSE)

```
Initial state (capacity 3):
[ ][ ][ ]

After pushing 100, 200, 300:
[100][200][300]  <- Full
 ↑           ↑
oldest    newest

After pushing 400 (shifts and overwrites):
Step 1: PopLeft removes 100
[200][300][ ]

Step 2: AppendRight adds 400
[200][300][400]
 ↑           ↑
oldest    newest

After pushing 500:
[300][400][500]
 ↑           ↑
oldest    newest
```

### Advantages
- **Consistent indexing**: Elements always occupy contiguous indices starting from 0
- **Configurable direction**: Can optimize for prepend or append patterns
- **Automatic capacity management**: Always maintains most recent N elements
- **Predictable memory layout**: No internal index tracking, uses actual array positions
- **Clean implementation**: Private helper methods separate concerns

### Use Cases
- **Directional data streams**: Logs that grow in specific direction
- **Time-series data**: Keep most recent N samples with natural ordering
- **Event history**: Maintain fixed-size event list with temporal ordering
- **Undo/redo buffers**: Limited-size command history
- **Message queues**: Fixed-size message buffers with FIFO ordering

### Comparison with Other Adapters

| Feature | FifoBuffer | RingBuffer | List |
|---------|-----------|------------|------|
| Overwrite when full | No (fails) | Yes | Yes |
| Fill direction | Fixed | Fixed | Configurable |
| Physical shifting | Always | On overwrite | On overwrite |
| Index stability | No | No | Yes (contiguous) |
| Use case | Queue | Circular log | Directional list |

### Performance Considerations

**Fill From Left (fillFromLeft = TRUE)**:
- **Push (not full)**: O(n) - AppendLeft shifts all elements
- **Push (full)**: O(n) - PopRight + AppendLeft, double shift
- **Pop**: O(1) - PopRight removes last element

**Fill From Right (fillFromLeft = FALSE)**:
- **Push (not full)**: O(1) - AppendRight adds to end
- **Push (full)**: O(n) - PopLeft shifts + AppendRight
- **Pop**: O(n) - PopLeft shifts remaining elements

**Recommendation**: Set fillFromLeft based on your access pattern:
- Frequent pushes, infrequent pops: fillFromLeft = FALSE (O(1) push)
- Frequent pops, infrequent pushes: fillFromLeft = TRUE (O(1) pop)

### Private Helper Methods

The implementation uses private helper methods for code organization:
- `pushInternal()`: Encapsulates push logic with direction handling
- `popInternal()`: Encapsulates pop logic with direction handling
- `removeOldest()`: Removes oldest element based on fill direction

This separation improves:
- Code readability and maintainability
- Testability of individual operations
- Reusability of common logic

### Dependencies
- Requires I_AnyBuffer implementation (e.g., AnyBuffer)
- Uses Trace for error logging and verbose diagnostics
- Implements I_AnyBufferStrategy interface

### Related Patterns
- **FifoBuffer**: FIFO without overwrite, fixed left-to-right fill
- **RingBuffer**: Circular buffer with overwrite, fixed fill direction
- **LifoBuffer**: Stack (Last-In-First-Out) semantics
*)
]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
    <Method Name="Clear" Id="{fa333a0f-dfce-409d-83ec-9b28b57f79f1}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Removes all elements from the list and resets to empty state
METHOD Clear : BOOL

(*
## Detailed Description

Clears all elements from the underlying buffer, resetting it to an empty state.
After calling Clear, isEmpty will return TRUE and elementCount will be 0.

This operation delegates directly to the underlying anyBuffer.Clear() method.

### Return Value
- **TRUE**: List was successfully cleared
- **FALSE**: Clear operation failed (e.g., anyBuffer is not initialized)

### Side Effects
- All elements are removed from the buffer
- Element count is reset to 0
- Buffer capacity is restored to maximum
- Logs verbose trace message on success
*)
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[Clear := FALSE;
IF anyBuffer <> 0 THEN
	Clear := anyBuffer.Clear();
END_IF

Trace.Verbose(__POUNAME(), 'executed');]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="FB_Init" Id="{83462b9f-5de2-49c5-b255-d1249675cfda}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Initializes the list by injecting the underlying buffer dependency
METHOD FB_Init : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
	bInitRetains : BOOL;		  // TRUE: the retain variables are initialized (reset warm / reset cold)
	bInCopyCode	 : BOOL;		  // TRUE: the instance will be copied to the copy code afterward (online change)
	anyBuffer	 : I_AnyBuffer;	  // The underlying buffer implementation to wrap
	fillFromLeft : BOOL := FALSE; // TRUE: fill from left (prepend), FALSE: fill from right (append)
END_VAR

(*
## Detailed Description

Initializes the List by injecting the underlying AnyBuffer dependency and configuring
the fill direction. This follows the dependency injection pattern where the buffer
implementation and behavior are provided during construction.

### Initialization Sequence
1. Validates that a valid anyBuffer reference is provided (non-zero pointer)
2. Stores the buffer reference for use by Push, Pop, and other operations
3. Stores the fillFromLeft flag to control insertion direction
4. Sets isInitialized flag to TRUE to enable operations

### Parameters
- **anyBuffer**: Reference to an I_AnyBuffer implementation (e.g., AnyBuffer instance)
  - Must be a valid, initialized buffer
  - This List will delegate all operations to this buffer
- **fillFromLeft**: Controls insertion direction and FIFO ordering
  - **FALSE** (default): Fill from right - AppendRight for push, PopLeft for pop
    - Newest elements at high indices, oldest at index 0
    - Optimized for frequent pushes (O(1))
  - **TRUE**: Fill from left - AppendLeft for push, PopRight for pop
    - Newest elements at index 0, oldest at high indices
    - Optimized for frequent pops (O(1))

### Return Value
Returns BOOL but value is not evaluated by the runtime. Always call with valid anyBuffer.

### Usage Example - Append Mode (fillFromLeft = FALSE)
```iecst
VAR
    rawBuffer : ARRAY[0..9] OF DINT;
    buffer : AnyBuffer(pBuffer := rawBuffer,
                       bufferBoundLower := 0,
                       bufferBoundUpper := 9,
                       isBufferPersistent := FALSE);
    list : List(anyBuffer := buffer,
                fillFromLeft := FALSE);  // Append mode (default)
END_VAR
// Push is O(1), Pop is O(n)
```

### Usage Example - Prepend Mode (fillFromLeft = TRUE)
```iecst
VAR
    rawBuffer : ARRAY[0..9] OF DINT;
    buffer : AnyBuffer(pBuffer := rawBuffer,
                       bufferBoundLower := 0,
                       bufferBoundUpper := 9,
                       isBufferPersistent := FALSE);
    list : List(anyBuffer := buffer,
                fillFromLeft := TRUE);  // Prepend mode
END_VAR
// Push is O(n), Pop is O(1)
```

### Important Notes
- Must provide a valid anyBuffer reference, otherwise Push/Pop will fail
- The underlying buffer must already be initialized before passing to FB_Init
- Choose fillFromLeft based on your access pattern for optimal performance
- The fill direction cannot be changed after initialization
*)
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[IF anyBuffer <> 0 THEN
	THIS^.anyBuffer := anyBuffer;
	THIS^._reversed := fillFromLeft;
	isInitialized	:= TRUE;
END_IF]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Property Name="isEmpty" Id="{1546d14a-9d84-433b-b38f-10e25d7e2f67}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Returns TRUE if the list contains no elements
PROPERTY isEmpty : BOOL

(*
## Detailed Description

Returns TRUE if the list is empty (contains no elements), FALSE otherwise.
This property delegates directly to the underlying anyBuffer.isEmpty property.

Use this property to check if Pop operation would succeed before attempting to
remove an element.

### Return Value
- **TRUE**: List is empty (elementCount = 0)
- **FALSE**: List contains one or more elements

### Usage Example
```iecst
IF NOT list.isEmpty THEN
    list.Pop(value);  // Safe to pop
END_IF
```
*)
]]></Declaration>
      <Get Name="Get" Id="{5d99d15d-b604-4b07-a847-948033d3255f}">
        <Declaration><![CDATA[]]></Declaration>
        <Implementation>
          <ST><![CDATA[isEmpty := anyBuffer.isEmpty;]]></ST>
        </Implementation>
      </Get>
    </Property>
    <Property Name="isFull" Id="{e3e76755-6837-4c71-b951-d839fc5464da}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Returns TRUE if the list is at maximum capacity
PROPERTY isFull : BOOL

(*
## Detailed Description

Returns TRUE if the list is full (at maximum capacity), FALSE otherwise.
This property delegates directly to the underlying anyBuffer.isFull property.

Note: Push will still succeed when isFull is TRUE by automatically removing the
oldest element and shifting remaining elements. This property is informational
and indicates when the next Push will trigger shift-and-overwrite behavior.

### Return Value
- **TRUE**: List is full (elementCount = capacity)
- **FALSE**: List has space for more elements

### Usage Example
```iecst
IF list.isFull THEN
    // Next Push will remove oldest element and shift
    Trace.Info('List', 'Next push will overwrite oldest element');
END_IF

value := 100;
success := list.Push(value);  // Will succeed even if full
```
*)
]]></Declaration>
      <Get Name="Get" Id="{f50c4197-03f3-40ff-8cf7-e834bf1be49f}">
        <Declaration><![CDATA[]]></Declaration>
        <Implementation>
          <ST><![CDATA[isFull := anyBuffer.isFull;]]></ST>
        </Implementation>
      </Get>
    </Property>
    <Method Name="Pop" Id="{97a570d6-a61f-46fe-a6fa-0b4b5c4633ea}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Removes and retrieves the oldest element from the list (FIFO dequeue)
{attribute 'hasanytype'}
METHOD Pop : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
	element : ANY; // Variable to receive the popped element
END_VAR

(*
## Detailed Description

Removes and retrieves the oldest element from the list following FIFO (First-In-First-Out)
semantics. The location of the oldest element depends on the fillFromLeft configuration:
- fillFromLeft = TRUE: Oldest at end (highest index), uses PopRight
- fillFromLeft = FALSE: Oldest at front (index 0), uses PopLeft

This method delegates to the private popInternal() helper method for implementation.

### Operation by Fill Direction

**Fill From Left (fillFromLeft = TRUE)**:
- Oldest element is at highest index (end of list)
- Uses PopRight to remove (O(1) operation)
- No shifting required

**Fill From Right (fillFromLeft = FALSE)**:
- Oldest element is at index 0 (front of list)
- Uses PopLeft to remove (O(n) operation)
- All remaining elements shift one position left

### Return Value
- **TRUE**: Element was successfully popped and copied to element parameter
- **FALSE**: Pop operation failed (see error conditions)

### Error Conditions
- Returns FALSE and logs error if buffer was not initialized
- Returns FALSE and logs error if element size doesn't match buffer element size
- Returns FALSE and logs error if list is empty (no elements to pop)
- Returns FALSE and logs error if underlying pop operation fails

### Parameters
- **element**: Must be a writable variable (not a literal) of the correct size
  - Must match the buffer's configured element size
  - Will receive the popped element value on success

### Side Effects
- Removes one element from the list
- May shift remaining elements (fillFromLeft = FALSE)
- Decrements element count by 1
- Increases available capacity by 1
- Logs verbose trace message on success
- Logs error trace message on failure

### Performance
- **fillFromLeft = TRUE**: O(1) - removes from end, no shifting
- **fillFromLeft = FALSE**: O(n) - removes from front, shifts all remaining elements
*)
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[Pop := FALSE;
IF NOT isInitialized THEN
	Trace.Error(__POUNAME(), 'Buffer was not initialized yet, execute method .init() at least once');
	RETURN;
END_IF

// Valid sized element?
IF element.diSize <> anyBuffer.Configuration.elementSize THEN
	Trace.Error(__POUNAME(), 'Passed element to pop to is of improper size');
	RETURN;
END_IF

// Check if empty
IF isEmpty THEN
	Trace.Error(__POUNAME(), 'Attempt to pop from empty buffer');
	RETURN;
END_IF

// pop element based on fill direction
IF _reversed THEN
	// Fill from left: oldest element is at the end (highest index)
	Pop := anyBuffer.PopRight(element);
ELSE
	// Fill from right: oldest element is at the front (index 0)
	Pop := anyBuffer.PopLeft(element);
END_IF

// Trace result
IF Pop THEN
	Trace.Verbose(__POUNAME(), 'executed');
ELSE
	Trace.Error(__POUNAME(), 'FAILED');
END_IF]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="Push" Id="{863b8d3a-61d1-4d2e-bdfb-6c52d1123b9b}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Adds a new element to the list with automatic shift-and-overwrite when full
{attribute 'hasanytype'}
METHOD Push : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
	element : ANY; // Element to add to the list
END_VAR

(*
## Detailed Description

Adds a new element to the list. The insertion location depends on the fillFromLeft
configuration:
- fillFromLeft = TRUE: Adds at front (index 0) using AppendLeft
- fillFromLeft = FALSE: Adds at end using AppendRight

When the list is full, the oldest element is automatically removed and remaining
elements are shifted to make space for the new element.

### Operation Sequence (Not Full)
1. Validates that the buffer has been initialized
2. Validates that element size matches the buffer's configured element size
3. Adds element based on fill direction:
   - fillFromLeft = TRUE: AppendLeft (insert at index 0, shift existing right)
   - fillFromLeft = FALSE: AppendRight (insert at end)
4. Logs verbose trace on success or error trace on failure

### Operation Sequence (Full)
1. Validates that the buffer has been initialized
2. Validates that element size matches the buffer's configured element size
3. Removes oldest element based on fill direction:
   - fillFromLeft = TRUE: PopRight removes from end
   - fillFromLeft = FALSE: PopLeft removes from front and shifts
4. Adds new element based on fill direction:
   - fillFromLeft = TRUE: AppendLeft adds at front and shifts
   - fillFromLeft = FALSE: AppendRight adds at end
5. Logs verbose trace on success or error trace on failure

### Fill From Left Example (fillFromLeft = TRUE)
```iecst
// Buffer capacity = 3
value := 100; list.Push(value);  // [100]
value := 200; list.Push(value);  // [200, 100]
value := 300; list.Push(value);  // [300, 200, 100] - Full

// Push to full: Remove 100 (end), add 400 (front)
value := 400; list.Push(value);  // [400, 300, 200]

// Visual: [newest=400, 300, oldest=200]
list.Pop(value);  // Returns 200 (oldest from end)
```

### Fill From Right Example (fillFromLeft = FALSE)
```iecst
// Buffer capacity = 3
value := 100; list.Push(value);  // [100]
value := 200; list.Push(value);  // [100, 200]
value := 300; list.Push(value);  // [100, 200, 300] - Full

// Push to full: Remove 100 (front), add 400 (end)
value := 400; list.Push(value);  // [200, 300, 400]

// Visual: [oldest=200, 300, newest=400]
list.Pop(value);  // Returns 200 (oldest from front)
```

### Return Value
- **TRUE**: Element was successfully pushed to the list
- **FALSE**: Push operation failed (see error conditions)

### Error Conditions
- Returns FALSE and logs error if buffer was not initialized
- Returns FALSE and logs error if element size doesn't match buffer element size
- Returns FALSE and logs error if underlying append operation fails

### Parameters
- **element**: Must be a writable variable (not a literal) of the correct size
  - Must match the buffer's configured element size
  - Value will be copied into the list

### Side Effects (Not Full)
- Adds one element to the list
- May shift existing elements (fillFromLeft = TRUE shifts right)
- Increments element count by 1
- Decrements available capacity by 1

### Side Effects (Full)
- Removes oldest element
- Shifts remaining elements (direction depends on fillFromLeft)
- Adds new element
- Element count remains at maximum capacity

### Performance
**fillFromLeft = TRUE (prepend mode)**:
- Not full: O(n) - AppendLeft shifts all existing elements right
- Full: O(n) - PopRight (O(1)) + AppendLeft (O(n))

**fillFromLeft = FALSE (append mode)**:
- Not full: O(1) - AppendRight adds to end
- Full: O(n) - PopLeft (O(n)) + AppendRight (O(1))

Choose fillFromLeft based on your access pattern for optimal performance.
*)
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[Push := FALSE;
IF NOT isInitialized THEN
	Trace.Error(__POUNAME(), 'Buffer was not initialized yet, execute method .init() at least once');
	RETURN;
END_IF

// Valid sized element?
IF element.diSize <> anyBuffer.Configuration.elementSize THEN
	Trace.Error(__POUNAME(), 'Pushed element is of improper size');
	RETURN;
END_IF

// If buffer is full, remove oldest element first
IF isFull THEN
	IF NOT removeOldest() THEN
		Trace.Error(__POUNAME(), 'Failed to remove oldest element');
		RETURN;
	END_IF
END_IF

// push element based on fill direction
IF _reversed THEN
	// Fill from left: add new element at front (index 0)
	Push := anyBuffer.PushLeft(element);
ELSE
	// Fill from right: add new element at end
	Push := anyBuffer.PushRight(element);
END_IF

// Trace result
IF Push THEN
	Trace.Verbose(__POUNAME(), 'executed');
ELSE
	Trace.Error(__POUNAME(), 'FAILED');
END_IF]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="removeOldest" Id="{9b9a6968-0181-48be-aba0-9e9c8d4bd84e}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[// Private helper method to remove the oldest element based on fill direction
METHOD PRIVATE removeOldest : BOOL
VAR
	dummyElement : ANYTYPE; // For discarding oldest element
END_VAR

(*
## Detailed Description

Private helper method that removes the oldest element from the list based on the
fill direction. This method is called by Push() when the buffer is full to make
space for a new element.

### Operation
- fillFromLeft = TRUE: Oldest at end (high index), uses PopRight
- fillFromLeft = FALSE: Oldest at front (index 0), uses PopLeft

The removed element is discarded as we only care about making space.

### Return Value
- **TRUE**: Oldest element was successfully removed
- **FALSE**: Remove operation failed

### Side Effects
- Removes one element from the list
- May shift remaining elements (fillFromLeft = FALSE)
- Decrements element count by 1
- Increases available capacity by 1
*)
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[removeOldest := FALSE;
IF _reversed THEN
	// Fill from left: oldest element is at the end (highest index)
	removeOldest := anyBuffer.PopRight(dummyElement, TRUE);
ELSE
	// Fill from right: oldest element is at the front (index 0)
	removeOldest := anyBuffer.PopLeft(dummyElement, TRUE);
END_IF]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>